1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,025
 Sales teams do not need another list of company names.

2
00:00:04,025 --> 00:00:06,115
 They need a reason to reach out.

3
00:00:06,115 --> 00:00:10,315
 Kliseer connects seller context, dated public signals, and reviewable outreach,

4
00:00:10,315 --> 00:00:15,220
 helping building-material and electrical suppliers decide where to focus next.

5
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:21,113
 For a supplier, prospect research means connecting several pieces: what we sell,

6
00:00:21,113 --> 00:00:24,678
 which companies fit, and what has recently happened.

7
00:00:24,678 --> 00:00:28,523
 A public permit can be useful, but it still needs context.

8
00:00:28,523 --> 00:00:32,123
 The challenge is turning that scattered information into a clear, defensible next

9
00:00:32,123 --> 00:00:36,403
 step, without pretending that activity equals buying intent.

10
00:00:37,633 --> 00:00:41,233
 Kliseer brings that work into one workspace.

11
00:00:41,233 --> 00:00:45,078
 Klise helps turn company information into a profile and target criteria that the

12
00:00:45,078 --> 00:00:50,783
 seller reviews. Seer surfaces prospects with dated evidence and explainable scores.

13
00:00:50,783 --> 00:00:54,968
 From there, the seller can inspect contacts, ask questions, and prepare an outreach

14
00:00:54,968 --> 00:00:58,828
 draft, while keeping control of the final decision.

15
00:01:00,033 --> 00:01:04,668
 For this walkthrough, we use Harborline Electrical Supply, a fictional distributor

16
00:01:04,668 --> 00:01:07,363
 serving New York and New Jersey.

17
00:01:07,363 --> 00:01:11,453
 The seller can upload company materials or describe the business in chat.

18
00:01:11,453 --> 00:01:15,918
 Klise prepares editable fields, including products and service regions.

19
00:01:15,918 --> 00:01:20,138
 Each setup section is reviewed separately before approval, so an AI suggestion does

20
00:01:20,138 --> 00:01:23,043
 not silently become an accepted fact.

21
00:01:24,267 --> 00:01:29,377
 Seer uses public permit sources from New York City, Austin, and Seattle.

22
00:01:29,377 --> 00:01:32,992
 It surfaces companies with a signal in the last year, then applies rules for

23
00:01:32,992 --> 00:01:37,672
 keyword matches, freshness, location, and target fit.

24
00:01:37,672 --> 00:01:40,262
 These factors produce a score and tier.

25
00:01:40,262 --> 00:01:43,262
 The language model does not assign those numbers.

26
00:01:43,262 --> 00:01:47,047
 This is prioritization based on observable evidence, not a prediction that a

27
00:01:47,047 --> 00:01:48,907
 company is ready to buy.

28
00:01:50,133 --> 00:01:55,218
 Here is a concrete historical example: Hivolts Electrical in Brooklyn.

29
00:01:55,218 --> 00:01:59,668
 In the November seventh snapshot, its score was sixteen out of twenty, or Tier S.

30
00:01:59,668 --> 00:02:04,588
 The cited November first permit describes temporary power and generator-hoist work.

31
00:02:04,588 --> 00:02:09,338
 That suggests relevance to an electrical supplier, but not a confirmed purchase.

32
00:02:09,338 --> 00:02:12,778
 Target fit was only one out of five, so the seller can see both the supporting

33
00:02:12,778 --> 00:02:15,113
 evidence and the limitation.

34
00:02:16,333 --> 00:02:20,573
 Once a prospect looks relevant, the seller checks the available contact and its

35
00:02:20,573 --> 00:02:25,413
 source. Kliseer can then draft a first-touch email using seller information and

36
00:02:25,413 --> 00:02:30,838
 dated signals. The message stays editable, and Kliseer does not send it.

37
00:02:30,838 --> 00:02:34,663
 Provider-supplied contact details are not treated as verified.

38
00:02:34,663 --> 00:02:38,373
 The seller still needs to confirm the recipient, the facts, and whether the

39
00:02:38,373 --> 00:02:40,328
 outreach makes sense.

40
00:02:41,533 --> 00:02:46,163
 The chat also works with the current workspace: the seller profile, top Seer

41
00:02:46,163 --> 00:02:49,618
 prospects, and sourced contact records.

42
00:02:49,618 --> 00:02:54,263
 A rep can compare candidates, ask who has available contacts, or identify promising

43
00:02:54,263 --> 00:02:57,518
 prospects that still need contact research.

44
00:02:57,518 --> 00:03:00,603
 Missing details should remain missing, rather than being filled with a

45
00:03:00,603 --> 00:03:04,158
 plausible-looking email address or an invented decision-maker.

46
00:03:05,367 --> 00:03:10,102
 Vultr is central to the backend, not just a place to host a page.

47
00:03:10,102 --> 00:03:15,152
 Cloud Compute runs the Next.js application and the scheduled public-data ingestion.

48
00:03:15,152 --> 00:03:19,582
 Supabase, deployed through Vultr Marketplace, stores profiles, conversations,

49
00:03:19,582 --> 00:03:24,992
 companies, and signals. Vultr Serverless Inference supports AI drafting and

50
00:03:24,992 --> 00:03:29,452
 contextual responses. The important separation is that application rules calculate

51
00:03:29,452 --> 00:03:34,757
 scores, while the model helps interpret and communicate the supplied information.

52
00:03:35,967 --> 00:03:40,977
 Three boundaries matter. A relevance score is not buying intent.

53
00:03:40,977 --> 00:03:44,737
 A sourced contact is not automatically a verified contact.

54
00:03:44,737 --> 00:03:47,572
 And a generated draft is not a sent email.

55
00:03:47,572 --> 00:03:51,637
 Kliseer makes these distinctions visible and keeps review with the seller.

56
00:03:51,637 --> 00:03:54,727
 That is the product's approach: assist real sales work without disguising

57
00:03:54,727 --> 00:03:57,407
 uncertainty as confidence.

58
00:03:58,633 --> 00:04:02,808
 The intended value is a more focused research workflow: understand the seller,

59
00:04:02,808 --> 00:04:07,423
 prioritize with evidence, and prepare a relevant first conversation.

60
00:04:07,423 --> 00:04:10,893
 We are not claiming measured revenue gains or hours saved.

61
00:04:10,893 --> 00:04:14,918
 Those are things to validate. The next evaluation should measure time to a reviewed

62
00:04:14,918 --> 00:04:19,363
 shortlist, evidence accuracy, and whether sales reps find the resulting drafts

63
00:04:19,363 --> 00:04:20,898
 useful.

64
00:04:22,133 --> 00:04:26,458
 Kliseer turns scattered business information into a reviewed path from context to

65
00:04:26,458 --> 00:04:31,268
 outreach. Built on Vultr, it helps suppliers understand why a prospect deserves

66
00:04:31,268 --> 00:04:33,998
 attention and what still needs checking.

67
00:04:33,998 --> 00:04:37,648
 That is Kliseer: know why, then make your move.

68
00:04:37,648 --> 00:04:38,893
 Thank you.
